cmu-tips-1 = Antagonist selection runs a pity system: every round you're opted in and go unselected raises your draw weight, up to a cap. Getting an antagonist resets it. The count updates quietly on your account at round end.
cmu-tips-2 = The fewer antagonists you have enabled, the harder your pull lands on each of them. Enabling everything spreads the same pull thin, so pick the roles you actually want to play.
cmu-tips-3 = Gasmasks fully block neomorph spores, and partial masks only block most of them. Open wounds block nothing, so patch up before you walk into a spore cloud.
cmu-tips-4 = The neomorph sporecaster rolls a 5% chance every 3 seconds to tear off a spore-proof mask. About a minute standing next to one is all it takes.
cmu-tips-5 = As a medic, triage before you sprint. Revive whoever the next ten minutes need, not whoever yells loudest. In a mass casualty event, a fellow medic is worth more than a rifleman.
cmu-tips-6 = Tank crews don't look before backing up. Don't stand behind a tank.
cmu-tips-7 = Light armor is for roles that expect little combat. If you plan to see the front line, medium and heavy armor pays for itself.
cmu-tips-8 = Check a body's health before you shock it. Every failed shock deals zap damage, and enough of them can push a marine past what a defib alone can fix.
cmu-tips-9 = Medics, use your voice. Point at bodies that need dragging, call for CPR, tell people what they need. Silence helps no one.
cmu-tips-10 = Tracers work both ways.
cmu-tips-11 = Xenos exist in a state of quantum entanglement. They are simultaneously everywhere around you and nowhere your light is pointing.
cmu-tips-12 = Armor piercing mags are for things with plates. Standard mags hit harder against anything unarmored, so pack a mix.
cmu-tips-13 = When someone yells 'CLEAR!' with a defibrillator, wait for the shock. When they yell it with a rocket launcher, run.
cmu-tips-14 = If you're alone and you find a skinned body, take a deep breath. It won't help, but it's the last calm thing you'll do.
cmu-tips-15 = Treat civilians well and they may share intelligence, supplies, or even their allegiance. Antagonize them and the same list works in reverse.
cmu-tips-16 = Never trust a synthetic you haven't seen in over 15 minutes.
cmu-tips-17 = You can ask a Working Joe to run simple tasks or go places. So can everyone else. Joe does not discriminate.
cmu-tips-18 = 'Death before dishonor' is what people say so their meaningless death sounded like it mattered.
cmu-tips-19 = Grenades start their fuse the moment you prime them, whether you've thrown them or not. Cook it to leave your target no time to run. Cook it too long and enjoy your new prosthetic.
cmu-tips-20 = If you don't know how your role works, ask. Nobody was born knowing how to load an OB.
cmu-tips-21 = Friendly fire, isn't.
cmu-tips-22 = Regular flares light your way. Marking flares mark targets. They are not interchangeable, so check the box before the push.
cmu-tips-23 = Buildings are real and it does hurt to crash into them with a vehicle. Usually more for the crew than the building.
cmu-tips-24 = Don't tell your squadmates you turned off your IFF. They'll find out soon enough.
cmu-tips-25 = Wear a gasmask. You never know when you'll need one, and when you do, something will be actively trying to take it off.
cmu-tips-26 = Read your lore primer. The information inside has won battles.
cmu-tips-27 = Table manners are a combat multiplier. A fork makes eating faster and far less of a face-first affair.
cmu-tips-28 = Don't use the console command to "quit smoking". We checked.
cmu-tips-29 = The Union of Progressive Peoples isn't just Russians.
cmu-tips-30 = Your jet isn't invincible, pilot.
cmu-tips-31 = The new colony jeep can be yours for a very reasonable price, assuming nobody audits the requisitions ledger.
